<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ shareholders to vote on Ansett deal.</title>
<headline>Air NZ shareholders to vote on Ansett deal.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air New Zealand Ltd said on Monday it would seek shareholder approval for its planned purchase of half of the Ansett Australia Group from TNT Ltd at an extraordinary general meeting on September 27.</p>
<p>It said major shareholder Brierley Investments Ltd had advised that it would support the resolution. BIL owns 42.5 percent of Air NZ and Qantas Airways owns 19.9 percent.</p>
<p>Air New Zealand said the Ansett deal, which is also subject to Australian government approval, involves a total investment of A$475 million. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
